(APIServer pid=66698) [atom 07:51:08] ATOM DeepSeek-V4: no DP attention on the vLLM plugin path, so each of the 8 TP ranks reads every request's full MLA latent and index plane each decode step. Native's --enable-dp-attention is worth 1.95x (concurrency 64) to 2.31x (128) of decode step time at ISL 115k; the cost falls to ~0 at short context. Not a misconfiguration -- the feature lives in ATOM's engine, which plugin mode replaces with vLLM's model runner.
(APIServer pid=66698) [atom 07:51:08] ATOM DeepSeek-V4: cudagraph_mode FULL_AND_PIECEWISE requests piecewise cudagraphs, but the model is ATOM-owned so vLLM compiles nothing and splitting_ops is empty -- a 'piecewise' graph would be the whole model, replayed for batches whose query-length structure differs from capture. Demoting to FULL_DECODE_ONLY; pass `-O.cudagraph_mode=FULL_DECODE_ONLY` to select it explicitly.
(APIServer pid=66698) [atom 07:51:08] ATOM DeepSeek-V4: prefix caching enabled with SWA recompute (roll back last 1024 token(s) per hit = 8 proxy block(s), win_with_spec=135, index_topk=1024).
